<title>USA: U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage applications fell 2.8 percent in the week ended January 24, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>The volume of applications to refinance mortgages rose 0.5 percent, while applications to purchase mortgages slipped 4.0 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index rose 11.7 percent, to 341.6 from 305.8 in the previous week.</p>
<p>The purchase index fell 0.2 percent, to 179.6 from 180.0 in the previous week.</p>
